&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to provide
cycle storage and adequate refuse storage. As such, it would pose harm on the
highway. As such, the proposed development is considered unacceptable and
contrary to:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policy T5 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policy BR9 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide
     Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policy DMT3 and&amp;nbsp;Part 3 in Policy DMSI 8&amp;nbsp;of the London
     Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19
     Submission Version, December 2021)&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Council&#x27;s Planning Advice Note on Waste and Recycling Provisions in
     New and Refurbished Residential Developments (dated 20/05/2021)&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
     &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-font-kerning:0pt;mso-ligatures:none;mso-fareast-language:
     EN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The proposed first-floor flat would fail to
meet the minimum required Gross
Internal Area (GIA) floorspace, bedroom size for the proposed twin room, and built-in
storage for a 3-bedroom/5-persons flat. The shortfalls would result in substandard
accommodation for all future occupiers. In addition, the wall separating single
and twin bedrooms is considered to impede on daylight and sunlight received by each
room and potentially causing concerns regarding ventilation and overheating.
Overall, the proposed development is considered to represent a poor quality of
accommodation and contrary to:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;

&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Technical housing standards – nationally described space standard
     (March 2015)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Paragraph 135(f) of the National Planning Policy Framework (December
     2023)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policy BP6 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide
     Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:
     12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;
     mso-font-kerning:0pt;mso-ligatures:none;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The proposed two storey side extension by
reason of its bulk, mass, siting, and design would unbalance the terrace row
and close off the openness of the junction between Bennett&#x27;s Castle Lane and
Link Way.&amp;nbsp; The development would therefore detract from the character of
terrace row and wider area, notably given its location within the Becontree
Estate&amp;nbsp;which is a non-designated&amp;nbsp;heritage asset. As such, the proposed development is considered contrary to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot;&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Paragraphs 131, 135, and 209 of the National Planning Policy
     Framework (December 2023)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policies CP2 and CP3 of the Local Development Framework (LDF) Core
     Strategy (July 2010)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policies BP2, BP8 and BP11 of the Local Development Framework (LDF)
     Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
 &lt;li class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Policies SP2, DMD1, DMD4 and DMD6 of the London Borough of Barking
     and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037 (Regulation 19 Submission Version,
     December 2021)&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-font-kerning:0pt;mso-ligatures:
     none;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
